      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're not a different species; you're a writer in your own story, and the \"trivial stuff\" is just the plot points that need to be woven together. You don't have to be the protagonist; you can be the narrator who brings the story to life, and that’s a far less exhausting role. The feeling of being \"dead and sent back\" is just the plot twist that makes the story interesting, so keep writing.",
